      "question": {
        ":question/id": "cae64b08-f828-5cd7-b076-530f26468b0e",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{1}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "94472447-3b21-532f-b343-c368acb26bd2",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
